          {
            "typeName": "notesText",
            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "Method: Data was taken in high schools in Java, and Sumatra islands in Indonesia by the first author. Local assistants were recruited from the universities and institutes in Indonesia (Atmajaya University, Sanata Dharma University, & Gadjah Mada University). It was a survey and all questionnaires were given with the consent of the schools, parents, and respondents.\r\nUniverse: Age of respondents are between 12-19 years old, all are Indonesians from three ethnic groups: Javanese (from Java), Batak (from North Sumatra), and Chinese (from Java and North Sumatra).\r\nDSA proof."
          },
